__pycache__/
*.pyc
ext/
/tmp/
native/native_learner
native/native_learner_*
# E53: cross-compiled per-model native_learner binaries under results/ are rebuildable from
# the committed contract_gen.h + native_learner.c + toolchain (scripts/61) -- no repository
# precedent for committing them (unlike the vmfb/contract/dump artifacts, which ARE the
# evidence). Matches the exclusion above, scoped to results/ so per-experiment dump/*.so
# (the deployed embedded ELF, which IS evidence) stays tracked.
results/**/native_build/native_learner_aarch64*
*.o
*.log
!native/results/*.log
# D55 (v0.32.1): the per-experiment allowlist that used to follow here silently excluded the
# cFS raw logs of E28, E29 and E29b -- their EVIDENCE docs cited files that were never in the
# repository while summary.json kept the tests green. Raw logs under results/ are evidence:
# allow them all, and let harness/contract_negative_tests.py::cited_raw_logs_tracked_cases()
# fail when a summary.json cites a log that is missing or untracked.
!results/**/*.log
# F9 (external review v0.15, EVIDENCE_v0.16_E22): these dumps used to be excluded here
# ("intermediate executable dumps ... copied next to them" -- true of the ELF/codegen.ll,
# not true of dump/ itself) -- but harness/contract_negative_tests.py's regression and
# negative-case tests REQUIRE --dump-dir to point at real files, so excluding them broke
# fresh-clone reproducibility (verified: 33/53 instead of the in-tree 107/107). Committed
# instead (~6.5 MB total, intermediate MLIR/LLVM-IR/bitcode/object files, nothing sensitive).
!results/e14_aarch64_qemu/**/dump/**/*.o
